WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:06.659
Besides order books, the XRP Ledger has automated market makers: pools that trade with anyone.

2
00:00:06.659 --> 00:00:09.575
Here is how they work, and who sets their fee.

3
00:00:11.275 --> 00:00:19.424
A pool holds two assets, for example X R P and a stablecoin, and prices every trade from the ratio of the two balances.

4
00:00:19.874 --> 00:00:24.951
When you trade, the ledger routes through order books and pools, whichever gives the better price.

5
00:00:26.651 --> 00:00:31.473
People who deposit both assets receive L P tokens: their share of the pool.

6
00:00:31.923 --> 00:00:40.925
Every swap pays a fee of up to one percent into the pool, and L P token holders vote on that fee, weighted by how many L P tokens each one holds.

7
00:00:42.625 --> 00:00:50.156
Anyone can bid L P tokens for the auction slot, which lets its holder trade at a heavily discounted fee for a period.

8
00:00:50.606 --> 00:00:57.298
NOSHASHI's Pool Governance screen shows the fee, who votes it and with what share, and who holds the slot.

9
00:00:57.298 --> 00:01:02.979
A pool whose fee is set by one large holder behaves differently from one with many voters.
